<article class="env-proposition" id="03VG">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/03VG">Proposition <span data-tag="03VG">64.27.3</span>.</a> Let $X$ be an integral normal Noetherian scheme. Let $\overline y\to X$ be an algebraic geometric point lying over the generic point $\eta \in X$. Then </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \pi _ x(X, \overline\eta ) = Gal(M/\kappa (\eta ))  \]
</div>
  <p> ($\kappa (\eta )$, function field of $X$) where </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \kappa (\overline\eta )\supset M\supset \kappa (\eta ) = k(X)  \]
</div>
  <p> is the max sub-extension such that for every finite sub extension $M\supset L\supset \kappa (\eta )$ the normalization of $X$ in $L$ is finite étale over $X$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Omitted. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>